{
  "description": "R14 + D26: each of the 4 views, in light and dark, switches appearance live (same pid and window id) and samples its opaque card, primary text and primary (default) button within ΔE 3 of the macOS 27 token colours, and Settings also its checked switch (the system accent); screenshots of all 8 states recorded",
  "requirement": "R14 (GPUI Phase 1), D26 (native macOS 27 look)",
  "notes": [
    "Expected colours come from design/ubilink-tokens.json via theme/convert.rs and the accent derivation (theme/accent.rs), with the accent pinned by the accent-blue.json fixture (the macOS default, #007aff) so the run does not depend on the host's accent. surface = color.windowBackground (light #ffffff, dark #1e1e1e), the opaque card each view paints inside the glass frame. text = color.label (black/white at 0.85) composited over that card: light #262626, dark #dddddd. primary = the primary (default) button's fill: #007aff darkened just enough for white 13 pt text to reach 4.5:1, #0072ef in both modes (D26 deviation). accent (Settings only) = a checked, enabled Switch: the system accent itself, #007aff. The values are written here, not read from design/, so the proof cannot move with the tokens. rc.6: Settings has no accent-filled button (a Notes-style form), so it reports no primary sample and the probe checks that instead.",
    "Where each sample is is the view's layout, so each view reports a region per sample in its state (view.theme_samples.surface/text/primary/accent, window points, README contract); the colour is the probe's. The surface and primary are region means; the text and the switch are the best-matching pixel in their region (glyph cores carry the colour, a 16 pt switch track cannot hold a 24 pt solid square).",
    "Same pid: the probe's own child process is still the one it launched (process: unchanged). Same window id: saved per view before the first switch.",
    "Screenshots go to ~/Library/Caches/ubilink-probe/shots/<run>/theming-<view>-<mode>.png (path printed at the end). Pixel and screenshot steps need Screen Recording: ENV-BLOCKED without it, never a FAIL.",
    "Each reported region must be at least 24 x 24 pt (STATE_REGION_MIN_PT, ruling R-q), so a view cannot point the probe at a token-coloured swatch painted for it.",
    "Fixtures give every view real content to theme: a captured link, the ranking corpus, two missing permissions (loaded just before onboarding: with Automation not granted, opening capture goes to onboarding instead, rc.4; capture and the browser open with all granted); and the accent."
  ],
  "setup": {
    "graph": "graph-ranking.json",
    "fixtures": {
      "capture": "capture-ok.json",
      "permission": "permissions-all-granted.json",
      "accent": "accent-blue.json"
    }
  },
  "steps": [
